hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19113","Yaqub narrated to us: my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Ibn Shihab al-Zuhri said: Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham narrated to me, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Zamaa ibn al-Aswad ibn al-Muttalib ibn Asad, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became gravely ill, while I was with him among a group of Muslims, he said: Bilal called for the prayer, so he said: Order one who will pray with the people. He said: So I went out and there was Umar among the people, while Abu Bakr was absent, so he said: Stand, O Umar, and pray with the people. He said: So he stood, and when Umar said the takbir the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard his voice, and Umar was a loud-voiced man. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then where is Abu Bakr? Allah refuses that, and the Muslims refuse; Allah refuses that, and the Muslims refuse. He said: So he sent for Abu Bakr, and he came after Umar had prayed that prayer, and he prayed with the people. He said: And Abd Allah ibn Zamaa said: Umar said to me: Woe to you, what have you done to me, O Ibn Zamaa? By Allah, I thought when you ordered me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had ordered you with that, and were it not for that I would not have prayed with the people. He said: I said: By Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not order me, but when I did not see Abu Bakr I saw you as the worthiest of those present to pray."
